WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.957
Why are some desert coasts foggy,

2
00:00:01.957 --> 00:00:04.790
while western Europe stays mild in winter?

3
00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:07.144
The answer is rivers inside the sea.

4
00:00:07.544 --> 00:00:09.506
Ocean currents are huge flows of water

5
00:00:09.506 --> 00:00:11.793
moving in a definite direction.

6
00:00:11.793 --> 00:00:13.372
They are set going by the Sun's

7
00:00:13.372 --> 00:00:14.754
heat, the wind,

8
00:00:14.754 --> 00:00:17.178
gravity and the Coriolis force.

9
00:00:17.579 --> 00:00:19.390
Waves are different.

10
00:00:19.390 --> 00:00:21.120
In a wave the water mostly stays

11
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.011
put, and only the wave moves on.

12
00:00:24.011 --> 00:00:24.766
In a current,

13
00:00:24.766 --> 00:00:26.610
the water itself travels.

14
00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:28.682
Because the Earth spins,

15
00:00:28.682 --> 00:00:30.365
moving water turns right in the northern

16
00:00:30.365 --> 00:00:33.210
hemisphere and left in the southern.

17
00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.497
That bends currents into giant loops in

18
00:00:35.497 --> 00:00:36.737
every ocean.

19
00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:39.517
Warm currents carry tropical water towards the

20
00:00:39.517 --> 00:00:40.585
poles.

21
00:00:40.585 --> 00:00:42.965
Cold currents bring polar water towards the

22
00:00:42.965 --> 00:00:45.624
equator, often along the west coasts of

23
00:00:45.624 --> 00:00:48.399
continents, where they bring fog but little

24
00:00:48.399 --> 00:00:49.279
rain.

25
00:00:49.679 --> 00:00:52.280
Surface currents hold only about a tenth

26
00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:53.847
of the ocean's water.

27
00:00:53.847 --> 00:00:55.832
The other nine-tenths moves slowly in the

28
00:00:55.832 --> 00:00:56.759
deep.

29
00:00:57.159 --> 00:00:59.202
Where warm and cold currents meet,

30
00:00:59.202 --> 00:01:00.479
the water mixes,

31
00:01:00.479 --> 00:01:02.918
and you find the world's best fishing

32
00:01:02.918 --> 00:01:03.858
grounds.

33
00:01:03.858 --> 00:01:05.911
Remember that link for GS One.

